arscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Smalltalk-80 \lang1032 : \lang1033 bits of history, words of advice.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li173\fi0\ri0\sb91\sa0\sl-178\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Bibliography: p.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li170\fi0\ri0\sb2\sa0\sl-178\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Includes index.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi173\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-178\slmult0\tx3206 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1. \lang1033 Smalltalk-80 (Computer system) I. Krasner,\line \expndtw1 Glenn. II. Title: Smalltalk-eighty.\line \expndtw-5 QA76.8.S635S58    \lang1032 1983       \lang1033 001.64'.25{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-8\lang1032 83-5985}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li10\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-178\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 ISBN \lang1032 0-201-11669-3}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li17\fi0\ri0\sb197\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Reprinted with corrections, June \lang1032 1984}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb142\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Copyright \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'a9\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  1983 \lang1033 by Xerox Corporation.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb113\sa0\sl-178\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 All rights reserved. No part of this publication may be reproduced, stored in a retrieval system, or transmitted, in\line \expndtw0 any form or by any means, electronic, mechanical, photocopying, recording, or otherwise, without the prior written\line \expndtw2 permission of the publisher. Printed in the United States of America. Published simultaneously in Canada.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2\fi0\ri0\sb132\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 ISBN \lang1032 0-201-11669-3}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li170\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 CDEFGHIJ-AL-8987654}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3750\margrsxn1463\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2230\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-302\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn6\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs44 Preface}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2242\shptop74\shpright6706\shpbottom74\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 8890}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li17\fi0\ri0\sb2551\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The Software Concepts Group of Xerox Palo Alto Research Center\line \expndtw0 (PARC) has been working on the problem of how to give users access to\line \expndtw6 large amounts of computing power. We have concentrated our efforts\line \expndtw3 on the study of software systems, rather than on the creation of specific\line hardware packages. Our method has been to develop a software system\line \expndtw5 called Smalltalk, to create applications in that system, and then, based\line \expndtw3 on our experiences developing the applications, to design the next sys-\line \expndtw5 tem. We have developed and used three major Smalltalk systems over\line the last \lang1032 10 \lang1033 years, as well as a few minor variations.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi238\ri22\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We have documented and released the latest of these systems, the\line Smalltalk-80 system. We published a description of the system and a\line complete specification of its implementation in the book, \i Smalltalk-80:\line \expndtw5 The Language and Its Implementation. \i0 This first book, however, does\line \expndtw3 not cover the use of the system or programming style for writing large\line applications in the system. These topics are covered in the forthcoming\line books \i Smalltalk-80: The Interactive Programming Environment \i0 and\line \i\expndtw5 Smalltalk-80: Creating a User Interface and Graphical Applications.\line \i0\expndtw3 Nor does the first book discuss implementation techniques beyond the\line \expndtw6 formal specification, which is the subject of this book, \i Smalltalk-80:\line \expndtw2 Bits of History, Words of Advice.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi235\ri36\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 To check the accuracy and the clarity of the first book, we invited a\line \expndtw2 number of groups outside of Xerox to build implementations of the\line \expndtw4 Smalltalk-80 system. Those groups uncovered problems with the writ-\line \expndtw6 ten description, and with the system itself, which we then corrected.\line \expndtw3 They   also   formed   the   beginning   of   a   community   of   Smalltalk}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1962\margrsxn1184\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx3960 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 212{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Finding Out About Messages and Methods}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5105\margrsxn2264\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-983\shptop306\shpright5756\shpbottom306\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 25400}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-983\shptop313\shpright-983\shpbottom5159\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 25400