hich\af0\dbch\f24\cchs161\lang1032 \'e7\hich\af0\dbch\af24\loch\f0\cchs161  \lang1033 a m e s}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1559\margrsxn1399\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx754 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 VI{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa533 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Preface}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1566\margrsxn1411\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1572\colsr670\colno2\colw6691 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-2\shptop-312\shpright8936\shpbottom-312\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 16510}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Acknowledg-\line ments}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li19\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We would like to thank the authors, their co-workers, and their organi-\line \expndtw7 zations for their contributions to this book, for their diligence during\line the release and review process, and for their willingness to be open\line \expndtw5 about the strengths and weaknesses of their Smalltalk-80 implementa-\line \expndtw4 tions. We would also like to thank the Xerox Research management for\line allowing us to release the Smalltalk-80 system, thus widening the com-\line \expndtw7 munity of Smalltalk implementors with whom we can share experi-\line \expndtw3 ences and insights.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li5\fi240\ri5\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Many people contributed to the production of this book. Each author\line \expndtw10 also acted as an editor of an early draft of another author's paper.\line \expndtw7 Janet Moreland helped coordinate this swapping with copying and\line \expndtw3 mailing. Doug Carothers answered legal questions. Ted Kaehler provid-\line \expndtw4 ed other bits of help, and Frank Zdybel added some words of his own.\line Dave Robson built the translator that allowed us to deliver manuscripts\line \expndtw3 electronically. Eileen Colahan of the International Computaprint Corpo-\line \expndtw4 ration was extremely cooperative and flexible in turning these electron-\line ic manuscripts into print. The cartoons in the book are by Ted Kaehler,\line \expndtw9 redrawn by Addison-Wesley artist Jean Depoian. Adele Goldberg\line merged the images into the cover design with help from Rebecca\line \expndtw6 Cannara. Particular thanks go to production editor Fran Fulton for her\line \expndtw2 cooperation and patience, and to Jim DeWolf and Cheryl Wurzbacher of\line \expndtw-2 Addison-Wesley.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi242\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Registered trademarks mentioned in this book are: AED-512, Ad-\line \expndtw6 vanced Electronic Design, Inc.; UNIX, Bell Laboratories; DEC,\line \expndtw0 DECSYSTEM, DECSYSTEM20, UNIBUS and VAX, Digital Equipment\line \expndtw5 Corporation; HP-IB, Hewlett-Packard; GPIB, National Instruments;\line \expndtw3 BitPadOne, Summagraphics Corporation; and Smalltalk-80, Xerox Cor-\line \expndtw2 poration.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3810\margrsxn1399\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb346\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3810\margrsxn1399\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1917\colsr4063\colno2\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-240\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Palo Alto, California\line June \lang1032 1983}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\