1514\margrsxn8282\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb590\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1514\margrsxn8282\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1105\colsr266\colno2\colw741 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1343\shptop18\shpright1343\shpbottom680\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 20320}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb497\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Figure 10.13b}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-590\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex79\expndtw-48\dn11\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs110 ra}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn682\margrsxn1521\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb580\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn682\margrsxn1521\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx0\posnegy0\absw0\absh1066\nowrap\dfrmtxtx10080\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw1054\pich1879\picwgoal597\pichgoal1065\jpegblip
}\par{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1370\margrsxn1647\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop-58\shpright4745\shpbottom-58\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex140\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 The Smalltalk-80 System Release Process}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2257\fi0\ri0\sb166\sa0\sl-259\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 system to the non-Xerox world. The stated purposes of this dissemina-\line \expndtw1 tion were to:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb353\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2718 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  1.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb353\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2718 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-19\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 expand the community of Smalltalk programmers in order to gain\line \expndtw4 more general experience with how people can use the language;}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2718 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2718 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 expand the community of programming language researchers who\line study aspects of the Smalltalk style of programming;}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx2718 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx2718 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 influence hardware designers to consider ways in which to provide\line \expndtw4 increased performance for the Smalltalk style of interaction; and}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2718 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  4.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2718\fi-259\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2718 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 establish a standard for Smalltalk as an object-oriented program-\line \expndtw3 ming language and a graphics-based, interactive program develop-\line \expndtw5 ment environment.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2228\fi0\ri0\sb432\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The dissemination was planned in three parts: a series of introductory\line \expndtw5 articles, a book giving detailed system specifications, and a magnetic\line \expndtw6 tape containing the system itself. The series of articles would provide\line \expndtw4 an early and less formal introduction to the Smalltalk-80 system. Ulti-\line \expndtw6 mately, these articles were published in the August \lang1032 1981 \lang1033 special issue\line \expndtw0 of \i Byte \i0 magazine. The system specification was divided into two major\line \expndtw4 components\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0\lang1033 the Virtual Machine and the Virtual Image. The Virtual\line Machine for a particular hardware system consists of an interpreter, a\line storage manager, and primitives for handling the input/output devices.\line \expndtw1 The Virtual Image is a collection of objects that make up descriptions of\line \expndtw7 classes providing basic data structures (including numbers), basic\line graphics and text, compiler, decompiler, debugger, and viewing and\line \expndtw10 user interface support. The Virtual Image contains approximately\line \expndtw2\lang1032 10,000 \lang1033 objects. The proposed book would contain the formal specifica-\line \expndtw3 tions for the implementation of the Virtual Machine, as well as a de-\line \expndtw4 scription of the language and the interfaces to the objects in the Virtual\line \expndtw2 Image. The proposed tape would contain a digital representation of the\line \expndtw7 Virtual Image that could be loaded into a hardware system on which\line \expndtw5 the Virtual Machine had been implemented.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2218\fi241\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 All systems running the Smalltalk-80 system would therefore look\line \expndtw4 the same; each would have to support bitmapped graphics and a point-\line \expndtw2 ing device for controlling a cursor on the graphics display. The issue of\line \expndtw4 protecting the software was resolved by copyrighting the Virtual Image\line \expndtw2 and publicly disclosing the Virtual Machine; licensing under copyright\line \expndtw4 grants the licensee the right to reproduce the Image only for incorpora-\line \expndtw3 tion into a hardware product of the licensee. Any unincorporated repro-\line \expndtw4 duction and distribution is prohibited. The modular approach to the\line \expndtw3 Smalltalk design made this form of protection feasible.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3492\margrsxn1740\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1937\shptop-22\shpright6682\shpbottom-22\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex143\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Introduction}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi238\ri14\sb263\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 An initial attempt to produce a book about the Smalltalk system de-\line \expndtw7 scribed the design of an unfinished system that was to be called\line \expndtw4 Smalltalk-80. Chapters of the book were written in the spring and sum-\line \expndtw1 mer of \lang1032 1979. \lang1033 Since much of this written material described how to im-\line \expndtw6 plement the system, an appropriate review of the material required\line \expndtw3 following the specifications and actually implementing the Virtual Ma-\line chine. This was accomplished by involving members of software groups\line \expndtw2 of several computer manufacturers in the process of review and imple-\line \expndtw3 mentation. Although the Smalltalk systems had received a great deal of\line \expndtw2 publicity since Smalltalk-72 was first designed, few people outside Xe-\line \expndtw5 rox's research centers had actually used them before this review.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi234\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The cautious invitation issued to six companies was to read the book\line \expndtw8 material in order to understand the nature of the system. Reviewers\line \expndtw5 were also invited to visit the Xerox Palo Alto Research Center in order\line \expndtw3 to see a live demonstration of the system. If they were still interested in\line \expndtw6 the system after reading the written material and participating in a\line \expndtw4 demonstration, they were invited to enter the second phase of review\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'97\line \expndtw6\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0\lang1033 an actual implementation. A company could only accept the invitation\line \expndtw9 if it had \lang1032 (1) \lang1033 the required hardware (at least a 16-bit processor, a\line \expndtw6 bitmapped display, and a way of indicating locations on the display),\line \expndtw3 and \lang1032 (2) \lang1033 a software team on the project that consisted of regular employ-\line \expndtw-1 ees only.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi238\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Only four of those invited were able to enter the second phase of the\line \expndtw5 review, Apple Computer, Digital Equipment Corporation, Hewlett-\line \expndtw7 Packard, and Tektronix. These four companies agreed to share in\line \expndtw2 debugging the formal specification of the Virtual Machine. Problems\line encountered and general design advice would be exchanged with all\line \expndtw5 participants. Besides assisting in completing a book about the system,\line \expndtw3 this review process would test the ability of these manufacturers to suc-\line \expndtw4 cessfully create a full implementation of the Smalltalk-80 system based\line \expndtw1 on the information provided in the book. Success would be measured by\line \expndtw7 each manufacturer's ability to "read and adopt" the Virtual Image; a\line \expndtw3 more subjective measurement would be the actual performance of the\line \expndtw6 system on each manufacturer's hardware.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi241\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 By \lang1032 1982, \lang1033 the review process was complete enough that a revision of\line the book was possible. Actually, the written material was treated much\line \expndtw3 the way the Smalltalk software had been treated over the decade of re-\line \expndtw1 search\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0\lang1033 it was thrown away, with the exception of the (now debugged)\line \expndtw2 formal specification of the Virtual Machine. All of the chapters were\line \expndtw4 rewritten. Because of the volume of material that was to be disseminat-\line \expndtw7 ed, the book became three books\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0\lang1033 one for the programmer and lan-\line \expndtw4 guage designer \i \{Smalltalk-80: The Language and Its Implementation),\line \i0\expndtw18 one for the user and programming environments designer\line \i\expndtw4 \{Smalltalk-80: The Interactive Programming Environment), \i0 and one for}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2202\margrsxn2000\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx3982 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex134\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 212{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex134\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Finding Out About Messages and Methods}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn5029\margrsxn2024\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-670\shptop307\shpright6069\shpbottom307\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 29210}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-670\shptop317\shpright-670\shpbottom5165\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 29210}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-168\slmult0 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx1474\posnegy1008\absw1368\absh-506\dfrmtxtx38\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex111\expndtw8\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 Interval}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-168\slmult0 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx1474\posnegy1008\absw1368\absh-506\dfrmtxtx38\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0