e lookup routines begin their search in the class of the re-\line \expndtw5 ceiver. If the message being sent is not in this class, the search contin-\line \expndtw4 ues up the superclass chain until an inherited message is found. Our\line interpreter was modified to gather statistics on the depth of search re-\line \expndtw5 quired. The method lookup cache was not in use when these statistics\line \expndtw3 were collected. The data in Fig. \lang1032 10.4 \lang1033 was gathered while executing the\line \expndtw2 "macro" operations in class Benchmark.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi238\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 About half of all sends are to methods defined in the class of the re-\line \expndtw4 ceiver, requiring \lang1032 0 \lang1033 depth of search. Searches of depth \lang1032 1, 2, 3, \lang1033 and \lang1032 4 \lang1033 oc-\line \expndtw6 cur with roughly equal frequencies of about \lang1032 7.5% \lang1033 to \lang1032 15%. \lang1033 Relatively\line few messages require a search of depth \lang1032 5 \lang1033 or more, but one search of\line \expndtw2 depth \lang1032 9 \lang1033 did occur.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2608\margrsxn787\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb954\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2608\margrsxn787\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols5\colno1\colw4010\colsr1044\colno2\colw720\colsr0\colno3\colw968\colsr421\colno4\colw720\colsr0\colno5\colw720 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri68\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Depth       Sends}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-590 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1764 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2959 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4010 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li565\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex1