ols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb1310\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1701\margrsxn1312\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1731\colsr518\colno2\colw6645 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop-317\shpright8899\shpbottom-317\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0\sl-230\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Performance\line \expndtw-4 Measurements}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Performance measurements are included here to allow comparisons\line \expndtw6 with other Smalltalk-80 implementations. These measurements were\line \expndtw1 made on a single-user Motorola MC68000-based system with the system\line \expndtw3 clock running at \lang1032 5 \lang1033 MHz. (A 4-byte register-to-register add takes \lang1032 1.6 \lang1033 mi-\line \expndtw1 croseconds. A 4-byte move from an absolute memory location to a regis-\line \expndtw2 ter takes \lang1032 3.2 \lang1033 microseconds. CPU memory accesses and display memory\line \expndtw4 accesses are synchronized, slowing the CPU by \lang1032 10-15%). \lang1033 The measure-}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1332\margrsxn1642\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4158\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5591\tlul\tx8615 \f2\fs20{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 .{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-10 187}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri43\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Acknowledgments}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2236\fi0\ri43\sb198\sa0\sl-227\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ments are a snapshot of work in progress as of July \lang1032 1982. \lang1033 The only ma-\line \expndtw2 jor optimization in use was a 256-entry message lookup cache. The\line \expndtw4 uninterpreted results of running Benchmark testStandardTests are re-\line ported in Chapter \lang1032 9.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2239\fi238\ri43\sb25\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A traditional test of system performance is the number of bytecodes\line \expndtw3 per second the system can execute. Bytecodes vary tremendously in\line complexity, from simple operations such as pushing a literal zero on the\line stack or branching to another bytecode to very complex primitive oper-\line \expndtw1 ations such as floating-point divide, string-to-string copy, or BitBIt oper-\line \expndtw3 ations. Therefore, bytecode-per-second measurements are extremely\line \expndtw2 dependent on the methods being executed. We had no trouble collecting\line measurements ranging from \lang1032 5000 \lang1033 to about \lang1032 30,000 \lang1033 bytecodes per second.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2236\fi238\ri43\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Our analysis was done by modifying the virtual machine to count the\line \expndtw4 actual number of bytecodes executed. This introduced an overhead of\line \expndtw3 about \lang1032 5%, \lang1033 which is compensated for in the final column of Table \lang1032 10.8.\line \expndtw1\lang1033 Class Benchmark, method test:labeled:repeated: was also modified to al-\line \expndtw3 low collection of the bytecode counts. We have chosen to report data\line collected for each of the "macro" operations in class Benchmark. Mea-\line \expndtw4 surements reported are the average of three trials. The message lookup\line \expndtw5 cache was in use when these measurements were taken.}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa918\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-338 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6674 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li644\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 10.8 \lang1033 Bytecodes/Second for Benchmark Macro Tests}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-482 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2160 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3247 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4392 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5515 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6674 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li572\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Activity}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li133\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Counts}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 ms Elapsed}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Bytecodes/sec}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri270\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 + 5%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-302 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2160 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3247 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4392 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5515 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6674 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 compile dummy method}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri94\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 550,061}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri230\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 49,440}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri169\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 11,126}\cell \pard \pl