on (realized with reference counts),}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bytecode decoding,}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Bitmap manipulation (BitBIt)\super 2\nosupersub ,}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Allocating and freeing objects,}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Object table (OT) indirections, and}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li277\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx479 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent202\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Method lookup.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li40\fi0\ri18\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We measured the cost of each activity by writing test programs in C\super 3\line \nosupersub\expndtw9 that simply looped and performed the operations as defined by the\line \expndtw2 book. The CPU execution times of these programs were compared with\line \expndtw4 dummy programs that looped without performing the measured opera-\line \expndtw6 tion. Although we never implemented a complete interpreter by-the-\line \expndtw3 book, we coded these key operations with as much ingenuity as those in\line \expndtw2 BS. In this way, we hoped to measure only differences caused by under-\line \expndtw9 lying data structures rather than those attributable to clever "hacks"\line \expndtw2 in the code.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li36\fi238\ri25\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Next, we derived a bytecode mix from a profile of a typical interac-\line \expndtw0 tive session of seven million bytecodes\super 4\nosupersub . This mix is shown in Table \lang1032 11.2\line \expndtw-5\lang1033 below.}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa407\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-331 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1915 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2887 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li875