brdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7525 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Fraction spent counting}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li281\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 40%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 11%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li637\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 3.6}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1601\margrsxn749\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li65\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5231 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 196{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li54\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa565 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex124\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Berkeley Smalltalk: Who Knows Where the Time Goes?}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1630\margrsxn1376\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1123\colsr1127\colno2\colw6652 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop-241\shpright8910\shpbottom-241\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Bytecode\line \expndtw-2 Decoding}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The definition of bytecode decoding encompasses the computation\line \expndtw1 performed identically for each bytecode. Both Dolphin and Dorado con-\line \expndtw3 tain fast hardware to decode bytecodes, a luxury absent from a conven-\line \expndtw4 tional computer like our VAX. In addition to the decoding itself, we\line \expndtw1 included checking for process switches, fetching bytecodes, updating the\line \expndtw3 virtual instruction pointer, and for BS, counting bytecodes. BS uses a\line \expndtw1 256-way branch table to decode single-byte bytecodes completely. We\line \expndtw2 combined the check for process switching and input polling into a single\line \expndtw3 counter that is decremented and tested for each bytecode executed. Al-\line though we did not measure this optimization by itself, we did duplicate\line the code for the directly executed primitives so they could be executed\line \expndtw2 in-line. Open coding minimizes the number of subroutine calls; the most\line \expndtw10 common bytecodes and primitives use none. We timed bytecode\line \expndtw1 decoding for both BS and a by-the-book implementation. As Table \lang1032 11.7\line \expndtw3\lang1033 shows, fast dispatching is critical\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0\lang1033 BS would be \lang1032 2.5 \lang1033 times slower with-\line \expndtw2 out it.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1601\margrsxn749\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard\plain\fs2\sa274\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-324 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3680 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4969 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7309 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1757\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 11.7 \lang1033 Bytecode}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Dispatching}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-475 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2254 \clv