h40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2254 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3680 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4969 \clvertalt\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7309 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 mean time per bytecode}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 207\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li385\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 83\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161 8}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li526\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 2.5}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-389 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3680 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4969 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7309 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 % \b\lang1033 of time spent dispatching   \lang1032 60%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li396\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 12%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li522\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 5}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1601\margrsxn1383\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1706\colsr551\colno2\colw6667 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4\shptop-166\shpright8925\shpbottom-166\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 BitBlt}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop1228\shpright1897\shpbottom1228\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 2540}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb1408\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 Coping With an\line \expndtw3 External Display}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 BitBlt\super 10\nosupersub  is the workhorse of the Smalltalk-80 graphics system. It per-\line \expndtw5 forms all bitmap manipulation and text composition. The large amount\line \expndtw4 of computation for this operation makes it a prime target for optimiza-\line \expndtw7 tion. BS uses an external display, and must pay communication costs\line \expndtw4 for bitmaps as well as the computation costs.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri0\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We found three techniques to cut communication costs to our external\line display: fill recognition, delayed output, and reordered output.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri18\sb252\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Q \i Fill Recognition \i0 The bulk of the computation on bitmaps fills a\line \expndtw3 rectangular area with all ones or all zeroes\super 11\nosupersub . These area fill operations\line \expndtw5 involve \lang1032 21 \lang1033 times more bits than other, more complex copying opera-\line \expndtw3 tions. BS determines which invocations of BitBlt merely fill areas and\line \expndtw1 sends rectangle fill commands to the display for them. (BitBlt itself is\line \expndtw3 optimized for this case with special-purpose routines.)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1395\margrsxn1410\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li8384\fi263\ri0\sb0\sa302\sl-205\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw-3\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 197\line \ul0\expndtw13\lang1033 BitBlt}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1395\margrsxn1594\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1900\colsr346\colno2\colw6674 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb3078\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex109\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Measuring the\line \i0\expndtw-2 BitBlt \i Optimization}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Q \i Delayed Output \i0 Second, borrowing an idea from an HP version of\line \expndtw2 Smalltalk\super 12\nosupersub , when displaying text, our output routine does not send in-\line \expndtw1 dividual character-sized blocks of pixels until the completion of an invo-\line \expndtw5 cation of the text composition primitive, scanCharacters. At that point\line \expndtw1 BS sends a complete word-sized block.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li22\fi0\ri0\sb245\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\loch\af1\dbch\af25\hich\f1\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 \u9633\'3f\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  \i\lang1033 Reordered Output \i0 Third, when sending a bitmap to the display de-\line \expndtw3 vice, the middle goes separately from the left and right edges. Since the\line middle is an integral number of bytes, no shifting is needed to align the\line \expndtw6 pixels for the display device. Each row in the middle of the bitmap is\line \expndtw4 sent as bytes, not bits.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri4\sb223\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The only display optimization that can be easily compared to the speci-\line \expndtw4 fication in the book is the special purpose code for area fill. We meas-\line \expndtw2 ured the time to fill a \lang1032 1000 \lang1033 by \lang1032 1000 \lang1033 bitmap with the slow, general code,\line \expndtw4 and the time to fill the same bitmap with the fast code for zero and one\line \expndtw2 fill. The data in\super 13\nosupersub  supplied the proportion of work done by BitBlt (num-\line \expndtw4 ber of bits) that could be done with the special-purpose fast code. A\line \expndtw6 weighted average of the times then yields the mean time to fill a \lang1032 1000\line \expndtw4\lang1033 by \lang1032 1000 \lang1033 bitmap. Profile data supplied the midpoint proportion of total\line \expndtw0 time spent per bytecode on BitBlt. To derive the time spent in BitBlt per\line \expndtw5 bytecode for BS, we multiplied the time per bytecode by this percent-\line \expndtw4 age. We obtained the BitBlt time per bytecode of the unoptimized ver-\line sion by multiplying this time by the ratio of the unoptimized time to fill\line \expndtw5 a megabit to the BS time to fill a megabit. Table \lang1032 11.8 \lang1033 shows the results\line \expndtw3 of this calculation. We conclude that this optimization is important for\line \expndtw9 sessions that involve graphics and text composition, it doubled the\line \expndtw5 speed of the interpreter.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1395\margrsxn1410\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard\plain\fs2\sa194\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-338 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2498 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3873 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5097 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6667 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1480\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Table \lang1032 11.8}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 BitBlt \b Area Fill}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Optimization}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-482 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2498 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3873 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5097 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6667 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li389\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Measurement}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 By-the-book}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li180\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 BS}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 By-the-book/BS}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-259 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2498 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3873 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5097 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6667 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 time to fill \lang1032 1000 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'f7\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  1000}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-223 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2498 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3873 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5097 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6667 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li68\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 zeroes}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 2100m