161\lang1032\fs18 83\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161 8}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li259\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex105\expndtw-2\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161 2.1}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1627\margrsxn1372\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li43\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5216 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 198{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Berkeley Smalltalk: Who Knows Where the Time Goes?}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop346\shpright8921\shpbottom346\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb659\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2264 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Allocation and         \b0 Unix includes a library package for allocating and freeing areas of\line \b\charscalex142\expndtw-4\fs20 Freeing{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex113 memory\super 14\nosupersub ,   but   it   might   be   too   general   to   be   fast   enough   for   a}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2257\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Smalltalk-80 system. The proliferation of dynamic objects in a\line \expndtw1 Smalltalk-80 environment strains conventional memory allocators. In\line \expndtw2 particular, every message send and return pair results in allocating and\line \expndtw0 freeing a context object. Many Points are created and discarded in the\line graphics routines. The popularity of these two classes is shown in Table\line \expndtw-1\lang1032 11.9, \lang1033 the percentage of allocation frequency by size based on measure-\line \expndtw-14 ments\super 15\nosupersub .}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2254\shptop400\shpright8914\shpbottom400\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3409\fi0\ri0\sb457\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 11.9 \lang1033 Sizes of Frequently Allocated Objects}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa274\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-259 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx698 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2829 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4629 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Size}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li151\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Allocation Frequency}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Comments}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-281 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx698 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2829 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4629 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 18}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri835\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 84%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 size of small context}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx698 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2829 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4629 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri850\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 9%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 size of point object}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx698 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2829 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4629 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 28}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri850\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 size of large context}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-187 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx698 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2829 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4629 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 other}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri850\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 6%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2254\shptop101\shpright8914\shpbottom101\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2243\fi0\ri7\sb410\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 BS exploits this pattern with an algorithm outlined in the specification\super 16\nosupersub .\line \expndtw1 We observed that when a small object such as a context is freed, the\line \expndtw0 probability of an allocation request for an object of the same size in the\line \expndtw2 near future is high. The obvious strategy then is to hold onto the space\line \expndtw0 and OT entry for the freed object, and to recycle it for the expected al-\line \expndtw3 location. Although the specification defines a small object as one with\line \expndtw4\lang1032 20 \lang1033 or fewer fields, we extended it to \lang1032 40 \lang1033 to cover large contexts as\line \expndtw0 suggested by Peter Deutsch. For each size of small object \lang1032 (0-40), \lang1033 BS\line maintains a pool of free objects on a linked list. Thus BS can allocate a\line \expndtw1 small object by removing one from the appropriate list, setting its class\line \expndtw4 and reference count, and nilling out the object's fields. If a pool runs\line \expndtw2 dry, the Unix storage allocator is invoked to obtain a chunk of memory\line \expndtw0\lang1032 10 \lang1033 times the desired size. BS then divides the chunk into \lang1032 10 \lang1033 free objects,\line \expndtw4 and tosses them into the pool. If too many objects end up in the free\line \expndtw0 pools, it is possible to run out of available OT slots. When this happens,\line \expndtw3 OT entries must be released from the free objects. The memory space\line \expndtw1 for large objects is obtained from the Unix allocator.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2246\fi238\ri11\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 We measured the cost of an allocation with a test program that re-\line \expndtw-2 peatedly allocated and freed \lang1032 100 \lang1033 context-sized objects with a LIFO disci-\line \expndtw3 pline. Both the Unix allocator and the BS allocator were measured. It\line \expndtw1 will be useful for the analysis to trichotomize sends:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2740\fi-238\ri11\sb180\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw2\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 1. \lang1033 We call sends to methods that simply return self or an instance\line \expndtw1 variable \i short-circuit sends. \i0 The method header names the field to\line \expndtw3 be returned.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1359\margrsxn1597\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4194\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx7481\tlul\tx8669 \f2\fs20{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 .{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-10 199}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri11\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex111\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Object Table Indirection}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2776\fi-256\ri0\sb281\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2776 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2776\fi-256\ri0\sb281\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2776 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Other sends result in the invocation of runtime interpreter sub-\line \expndtw4 routines. These are the \i primitives.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2776\fi-256\ri0\sb112\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx2776 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2776\fi-256\ri0\sb112\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx2776 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The longest sends activate a new context and transfer control to\line \expndtw5 the target method. We call these \i full sends.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2275\fi0\ri18\sb234\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The frequency of full sends provided the context allocation frequency,\line and the total allocation frequency was obtained by dividing the number\line \expndtw2 of contexts allocated per bytecode by the fraction of context allocations.\line \expndtw3 The allocate, free, and nilling out time is just the product of the alloca-\line \expndtw4 tions per bytecode and the time per allocation. Table \lang1032 11.10 \lang1033 shows this\line \expndtw3 calculation. Our object allocation strategy bought only a modest im-\line \expndtw7 provement in overall performance. The Unix allocator is well-tuned,\line \expndtw5 and the time allocating and freeing objects is amortized over the time\line \expndtw3 spent using the objects.}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa400\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-331 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1242\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 11.10 \lang1033 Cost}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 to Allocate and}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Free Object}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-468 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li605\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Measurement}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Unix allocator}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 BS allocator}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li86\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex111\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Unix/BS}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-310 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 time to allocate and free}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 130\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 21\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li61\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 6.2}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-245 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 time to nil out object}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 19\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 19\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li68\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1.0}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Total}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 149\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 40\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li58\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 3.7}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 allocations per bytecode}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 .13}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 .13}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li68\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 alloc/free/nil time per bytecode}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-11\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 19\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 5.2\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161 8}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li61\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 3.7}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 mean time per bytecode}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 97\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 83\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li68\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1.2}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-223 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Fraction of time spent}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-317 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2830 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4277 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5566 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6689 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li65\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 allocating}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 20%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 6%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 3.2}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2268\fi0\ri29\sb274\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There are more tasks involved in storage management than just allo-\line \expndtw4 cating and freeing, but the large address space and physical memory of\line \expndtw8 the VAX reduce the importance of most of them. BS usually needs\line \expndtw5 about half a megabyte of physical memory, and fits comfortably on our\line \expndtw3\lang1032 4 \lang1033 megabyte time-shared VAX. In particular, we have not observed any\line \expndtw4 thrashing, and thus have ignored dynamic compaction. Garbage collec-\line tion flashes by so quickly on a 32-bit computer with plentiful memory\line \expndtw5 that it can be hidden in the time needed to save an image on disk.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop828\shpright8924\shpbottom828\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb1145\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2264 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex127\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Object Table{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex100\expndtw6 To read or write a field of an object, the Smalltalk-80 virtual machine}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2264 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex127\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Indirection{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex100\expndtw7 must first determine the object's memory address from the Object Ta-}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri43\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 ble. We optimized this object table indirection just as we optimized ref-\line \expndtw6 erence counting. Addresses, like counts, are stored in a separate array,}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1523\margrsxn1491\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx1570 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 200{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw11\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Berkeley Smalltalk: Who Knows Where the Time Goes?}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2239\fi0\ri14\sb274\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 and the same Oop format that facilitates indexing the reference array\line \expndtw5 speeds accesses to the object address array. We used test programs to\line time the cost of an indirection. Indirection is so simple that the array\line \expndtw7 access costs dominates; the data structures in the book would double\line \expndtw4 the time for each object table indirection on a VAX.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2236\fi241\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Close scrutiny of the book and the BS source code yielded the num-\line \expndtw2 ber of indirections. BS avoids object table indirections by saving memo-\line \expndtw6 ry addresses of some objects in registers. In particular, it keeps the\line \expndtw9 current receiver, active and home contexts, current method, top of\line \expndtw3 stack, and next bytecode addresses in registers or local variables. Those\line \expndtw4 primitives and bytecodes that do multiword transfers or read-modify-\line \expndtw5 write operations also keep addresses in registers. Scattering addresses\line \expndtw2 around in registers complicates compaction, but except for garbage col-\line \expndtw3 lection, BS does not compact. Tables \lang1032 11.11 \lang1033 and \lang1032 11.12 \lang1033 enumerate the in-\line \expndtw9 directions performed for a full send and a return, respectively. The\line \expndtw3 need to recursively free the old context increases the number of indirec-\line \expndtw4 tions for a by-the-book return.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2239\shptop623\shpright8899\shpbottom623\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3222\fi0\ri0\sb680\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 11.11 \lang1033 Object Table Indirections for Full Sends}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa274\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-259 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2844 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4637 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5047 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li695\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Operation}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li414\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 By-the-book}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li158\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 \'c2}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-281 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2844 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4637 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5047 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 fetch send}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li817\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 1}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li205\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 0}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-245 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2844 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4637 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5047 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 copy receiver and argument}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li806\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\c