d programming tricks\line \expndtw1 speed recursive freeing and garbage collection for certain popular clas-\line \expndtw2 ses. Subroutine calls and other overhead are trimmed in sends and re-\line \expndtw7 turns. Floating point arithmetic is performed in hardware. Most of\line \expndtw2 these optimizations are easily discovered and are unrelated to the\line \expndtw1 distinguishing characteristics of the Smalltalk-80 system.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1395\margrsxn765\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop486\shpright8928\shpbottom486\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb810\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2272 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex141\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Other{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex113\expndtw3 As Table \lang1032 11.1 \lang1033 shows, the activities we measured account for a total of}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2275 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex141\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Interpreter{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex113\expndtw7\lang1032 40\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  \lang1033 per bytecode in BS. BS has been instrumented to measure the}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2272 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex141\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Activities{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex113\expndtw2 bytecodes executed per CPU-second; this is about \lang1032 12000 \lang1033 for typical in-}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2275\fi0\ri817\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 teractive sessions of browsing, editing, compiling, and so forth. Thus, BS\line spends \lang1032 1/12000 \lang1033 second or \lang1032 83\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'ec\'e2\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  \lang1033 per bytecode. That leaves 43jas unac-\line \expndtw1 counted for. This represents the "useful work", in the sense that it con-\line \expndtw4 tains no easy targets for optimization. It includes the execution of\line \expndtw0 bytecodes and primitives.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2279\fi238\ri814\sb0\sa943\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Although we have optimized these activities in the obvious ways (e.g.\line \expndtw0 open coding), these are the least interesting optimizations. We therefore\line \expndtw5 made the conservative assumption that the unoptimized interpreter\line \expndtw-2 would be no slower.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1395\margrsxn1586\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1537\colsr727\colno2\colw6663 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop-317\shpright8928\shpbottom-317\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb14\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Comparative}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Execution}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Times}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex113\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 How close is BS to an optimal Smalltalk-80 implementation? The\line \expndtw4 fastest Smalltalk-80 implementation is Deutsch's Dorado interpreter.\line \expndtw0 The Dorado is a powerful personal computer\super 17\nosupersub  with a microcycle time\line \expndtw1 three times faster than the VAX-11/780. The Dolphin is a more modest\line \expndtw0 machine; it is considered to be adequate but not comfortable. We decid-\line ed to examine two test cases: our typical interactive session and Baden's\line \expndtw3 Towers of Hanoi benchmark\super 18\nosupersub . Peter Deutsch measured the perfor-\line \expndtw2 mance of the Xerox implementations on the Hanoi benchmark. The\line numbers for the Xerox implementations for the typical interactive ses-\line \expndtw-1 sion reflect the best estimates of the Software Concepts Group. The exe-\line \expndtw1 cution  rate  for  BS  was  measured  as  described above.  Table   \lang1032 11.16}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1395\margrsxn765\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard\plain\fs2\sa443\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-331 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2434 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3658 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5012 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7582 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li482\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 11.16 \lang1033 Relative}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Performance}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 (kilobytecodes}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 per second)}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-482 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2434 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3658 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5012 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7582 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li371\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Case}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li446\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 BS}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Dolphin}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Dorado}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-288 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2434 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3658 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5012 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx7582 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Interactive use}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li457\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 12}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 30}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li94\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 400}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-324 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2434 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3658 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5012 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx7582 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Towers of Hanoi}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li443\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 23}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 33}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li90\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 420}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1512\margrsxn1477\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5213 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 204{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Berkeley Smalltalk: Who Knows Where the Time Goes?}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2239\fi0\ri32\sb266\sa1159\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 compares BS execution speed for the two test cases. Although BS per-\line forms well for a conventional machine, it suffers in comparison to the\line \expndtw2 Xerox personal computers.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1523\margrsxn1477\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1436\colsr821\colno2\colw6652 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop-248\shpright8914\shpbottom-248\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Conclusions}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We have several minor reservations about the results in this paper.\line \expndtw3 First, our methods yielded only rough approximations. We ignored the\line \expndtw4 effects of the VAX hardware cache hit rate on the running times of our\line \expndtw3 test programs. Bytecode frequencies can be expected to vary. Second,\line \expndtw4 major optimizations often have synergistic effects on code complexity\line \expndtw6 and execution time. Finally, we did not explore some important areas\line \expndtw2 (e.g. context changing overhead). The intended value of this work lies in\line \expndtw6 ranking the different optimizable areas and in quantifying the benefits\line \expndtw3 of optimization. For instance, it clearly shows that reference counting\line \expndtw4 remains a more promising target than allocation and freeing. These\line \expndtw3 measurements and calculations do however, reinforce the need to opti-\line \expndtw4 mize carefully and tune implementations of Smalltalk-80 virtual ma-\line \expndtw3 chines. When our optimizations in the measured areas were combined,\line \expndtw4 they resulted in a fourfold improvement in performance.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1512\margrsxn1480\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb1188\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1512\margrsxn1480\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1558\colsr691\colno2\colw6667 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop-306\shpright8924\shpbottom-306\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Acknowledg-\line \expndtw-1 ments}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We would like to thank the Software Concepts Group for creating the\line Smalltalk-80 system and bringing it out into the light of day. In partic-\line \expndtw4 ular, we owe our gratitude to Peter Deutsch who has offered both\line \expndtw6 quintessential and patient technical guidance, and to Adele Goldberg\line \expndtw4 who issued our entry visa onto the "Isle of Smalltalk". We thank the\line \expndtw3 students here at Berkeley involved with the Smalltalk project: Scott Ba-\line \expndtw4 den, Ricki Blau, Dan Conde, Tom Conroy, Dan Halbert, Ed Pelegri,\line \expndtw7 Richard Probst, and Steve Sargent have contributed hard work, data,\line \expndtw3 and insight to the task of understanding where the time goes. We owe a\line \expndtw5 debt of thanks to Jim Stinger, Ted Laliottis, Bob Ballance, and the rest\line \expndtw6 of the Smalltalk-80 group at HP Labs, who by permitting us to study\line \expndtw4 their unfinished implementation, furnished us with a working model to\line \expndtw6 study. Paul McCullough provided thoughtful and constructive com-\line \expndtw5 ments to help smooth out the rough spots in this paper.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi238\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This effort was funded in part by Apple Computer and the State of\line California through the Microelectronics Innovation and Computer Re-\line \expndtw2 search Opportunities program, and sponsored by Defense Advance Re-\line \expndtw-1 search   Projects   Agency,   Department   of   Defense,   Order   No.   \lang1032 3803,}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3745\margrsxn1518\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri14\sb0\sa0\sl-194\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex131\expndtw-15\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 205\line \expndtw1\lang1033 References}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb256\sa0\sl-187\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 monitored by Naval Electronic System Command under Contract No.\line \expndtw-4 N00039-81-K-0251.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-2275\shptop706\shpright6624\shpbottom706\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-241\ri0\sb1141\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx468 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-16\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  1.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-241\ri0\sb1141\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx468 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent241\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0