1 \lang1033 lists the static and dynamic frequencies of the Smalltalk-80\line \expndtw7 virtual machine instruction set. This distribution is remarkably uni-\line \expndtw4 form. Most dynamic instruction frequencies show at least one instruc-\line \expndtw8 tion at over \lang1032 10%\lang1033 \\ but the highest in the Smalltalk-80 virtual machine\line \expndtw13 is only \lang1032 6.48% \lang1033 for pushing a temporary onto the stack, usually\line \expndtw4 performed to work on an argument passed through the temporary vari-\line \expndtw2 able area. However, as the following section will show, there is some\line \expndtw1 regularity by category of bytecodes. The top \lang1032 17 \lang1033 bytecodes consume more\line \expndtw3 than \lang1032 50% \lang1033 of execution and the top \lang1032 34 \lang1033 are over \lang1032 70% \lang1033 out of \lang1032 247 \lang1033 designat-\line \expndtw-1 ed bytecodes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi230\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Pop stack top had the highest static frequency even though it was\line \expndtw3 ninth in execution. The top three bytecodes in static frequency comprise\line \expndtw4 one-fifth of all generated code. After that there is a steep drop and no\line \expndtw3 bytecode rises above \lang1032 3.39%. \lang1033 The less popular instructions tend to have\line higher static frequencies. Outside of the top \lang1032 30, \lang1033 the bytecodes have a\line \expndtw4 static/dynamic frequency ratio of \lang1032 4 \lang1033 to \lang1032 3.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi230\ri22\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 There are \lang1032 9 \lang1033 unused bytecodes in the Smalltalk-80 virtual machine\line \expndtw8 instruction set, and the system never executed \lang1032 18 \lang1033 other bytecodes in\line \expndtw7 our tests. Twelve of these instructions were long jumps, and all were\line \expndtw5 the longer varieties. The current Smalltalk compiler does not generate\line \expndtw7 the \i pop and jump on true \i0 instructions. This is apparently to simplify\line \expndtw4 the task of the decompiler. The other six untouched instructions were\line pushes and sends concerned with somewhat rare circumstances.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn896\margrsxn824\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li47\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5688 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-15\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 210{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li40\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 The Analysis of the Smalltalk-80 System at Hewlett-Packard}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2254\shptop335\shpright8900\shpbottom335\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri2632\sb385\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.2 \lang1033 Bytecode Frequency by Category}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn896\margrsxn2106\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2254\shptop36\shpright8900\shpbottom36\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft9634\shptop6674\shpright9634\shpbottom8524\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2311\fi0\ri0\sb230\sa0\tx5411 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Bytecode Category{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw2 Static \lang1032 %        \lang1033 Dynamic \lang1032 %      \lang1033 Cumulative}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-180 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx914 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3096 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri216\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 44.01%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri220\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 44.37%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li230\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 44.37%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx914 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3096 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri216\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 29.00%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri220\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 28.63%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li230\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 73.00%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx914 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3096 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri216\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 13.32%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri220\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 10.80%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li230\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 83.80%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-202 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx914 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2167 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3096 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri216\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 6.50%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri223\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 8.59%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li227\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5494\posnegy122\absw0\absh856\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 92.39%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2250\fi0\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 stack push}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2254\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 message send}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2254\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 stack pop and store}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2246\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 branch and jump}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2254\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx5587\tx6836\tx7920 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 return{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-7\lang1032 7.17%{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }7.61%{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }100.00%}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2246\shptop54\shpright8899\shpbottom54\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2254\fi0\ri0\sb317\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.2 \lang1033 groups the bytecodes into five categories for static and dy-\line \expndtw2 namic frequencies. The importance of message sends in Smalltalk is ev-\line \expndtw3 ident, but this can be misleading. The percentage of sends is so large\line because it includes both procedure calls \i and \i0 arithmetic and logical op-\line \expndtw7 erations (note the absence of a \i computational instruction \i0 category).\line \expndtw6 Also, because many of the sends are special or primitive operations\line which do not result in the execution of Smalltalk code, the percentage\line \expndtw4 of return instructions is much lower.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2257\fi238\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Stack operations account for \lang1032 55.17% \lang1033 of instructions executed, and\line \lang1032 71.37% \lang1033 are instructions other than sends. The frequency of stack push\line \expndtw3 and pop instructions points out the necessity of having an optimized in-\line \expndtw5 dependent path to the stack frame of the active context.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2257\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw14\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Although the message send is perhaps the most important part of}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx2257 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex119\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Send Bytecodes{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\i0\charscalex110\expndtw4 Smalltalk, it comprises only about one-quarter of execution time. More}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2246\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 importantly, nearly half are \i special \i0 sends which do not require a diction-\line \expndtw6 ary lookup for their selector. These special sends perform functions\line \expndtw4 which are typically in the instruction set of a processor, such as arith-\line \expndtw3 metic and logical operations for small integers.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2246\fi238\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Approximately every third instruction is a message send and sends\line \expndtw2 requiring dictionary lookups occur every \lang1032 6.67 \lang1033 bytecodes. Of the sends\line \expndtw3 needing dictionary searches, \lang1032 36.64% \lang1033 invoked primitives, and the rest\line \expndtw4 resulted in the execution of a Smalltalk method which, along with pro-\line \expndtw2 cess switches, accounted for a context switch every \lang1032 6.50 \lang1033 bytecodes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2236\fi241\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Of the special sends, \lang1032 78.92% \lang1033 are arithmetic and logical operations.\line \expndtw6 The remaining special sends fell further into the minority by a change\line \expndtw3 in the third test image release which required \lang1032 11 \lang1033 of the \lang1032 16 \lang1033 cases to look\line \expndtw8 up the selector in a special messages array rather than invoking a\line \expndtw4 primitive directly. As a result, some of these special sends actually re-\line \expndtw5 sult in the execution of Smalltalk code if the selector in the array does\line \expndtw6 not bind to a primitive for the receiver in question. Of course this al-\line \expndtw2 lows one to dynamically modify system behavior or to change this set of\line \expndtw6 primitives if future requirements should dictate. These other special\line \expndtw7 sends include high level operations such as instantiation, indexing,\line \expndtw4 length and class query, block evaluation, and point coordinates.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn896\margrsxn824\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li9468\fi0\ri0\sb734\sa0\sl-317\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn7\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs46 1}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3139\margrsxn2067\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4489\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Bytecode Measurements}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3139\margrsxn2092\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft11\shptop331\shpright6671\shpbottom331\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1098\fi0\ri0\sb389\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.3 \lang1033 Frequency of Message Sends by Flavor}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft18\shptop29\shpright6671\shpbottom29\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li86\fi0\ri0\sb241\sa0\tx2876\tx4468 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Flavor of Send{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6 Percentage{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 Cumulative Percentage}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-180 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1260 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2614 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3013\posnegy119\absw0\absh619\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 66.86%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3013\posnegy119\absw0\absh619\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 66.86%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1260 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2614 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3013\posnegy119\absw0\absh619\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 21.42%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3013\posnegy119\absw0\absh619\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 88.28%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-202 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1260 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2614 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3013\posnegy119\absw0\absh619\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 11.72%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3013\posnegy119\absw0\absh619\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 100.00%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 primitive}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 method}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 pseudo-primitive}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4\shptop58\shpright6657\shpbottom58\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb364\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 There are three flavors of message sends:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb194\sa0\sl-295\slmult0\tx2272 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Primitive{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\i0\charscalex100\expndtw0 Those which invoke C or machine code routines.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-295\slmult0\tx2268 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Method{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\i0\charscalex100\expndtw1 Those which activate Smalltalk code.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-295\slmult0\tx2272 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Pseudo-primitive{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\i0\charscalex100\expndtw3 Those which return directly after performing an operation}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2268\fi0\ri0\sb14\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 encoded in the header of the compiled method.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri22\sb241\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 The method sends are the best known of those in Table \lang1032 12.3. \lang1033 At about\line \expndtw2 one-fifth of all sends executed, this indicates the amount of optimization\line \expndtw1 possible through the proper choice of the set of primitives. The pseudo-\line \expndtw2 primitives, which offer an inexpensive way to access instance fields, ex-\line \expndtw4 ecute half as frequently as traditional method sends. In all, \lang1032 78.58% \lang1033 of\line \expndtw2 sends do not \i immediately \i0 result in the execution of Smalltalk code. This\line \expndtw4 does not take into account those primitives which fail and then activate\line \expndtw2 Smalltalk backup code (discussed later).}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft11\shptop378\shpright6664\shpbottom378\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li486\fi0\ri0\sb432\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.4 \l