dling.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1586\margrsxn1496\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx3895\tlul\tx5620 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 212{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex141\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 The Analysis of the Smalltalk-80 System at Hewlett-Packard}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2192\shptop292\shpright8823\shpbottom292\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3283\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.5 \lang1033 Failures of Primitive Methods by Type}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2185\shptop22\shpright8823\shpbottom22\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2203\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa0\tx5231\tx6836 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Type of Primitive{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6 Percentage{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 Cumulative Percentage}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2480\fi0\ri0\sb126\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx5382\tx7538 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 arithmetic{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6\lang1032 81.36%{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }81.36%}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2480\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx5393\tx7542 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 selector{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-8\lang1032 15.93%{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6 97.29%}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2480\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx5479\tx7456 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 common{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-7\lang1032 2.71%{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }100.00%}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2185\shptop54\shpright8823\shpbottom54\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2178\fi0\ri0\sb356\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Several interesting figures arise from Table \lang1032 12.5 \lang1033 which shows primitive\line \expndtw4 failures by type. Only \lang1032 4.49% \lang1033 of primitive operations fail, and most of\line these are the result of small integer arithmetic range violations. In fact,\line \expndtw5 arithmetic primitives are \i\lang1032 2.6 \i0\lang1033 times more likely to fail than selector\line primitives and \lang1032 8 \lang1033 times more likely than common primitives. The true\line \expndtw7 figure for arithmetic failures is probably even higher because we did\line \expndtw3 not implement certain primitives in the selector category (e.g., large in-\line teger arithmetic) and an invocation of one of them leads directly to a\line \expndtw5 primitive failure. Still the failure rate for arithmetic primitives is only\line \expndtw4\lang1032 6.49%, \lang1033 a testament to the utility of signed 15-bit arithmetic.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2178\shptop396\shpright8824\shpbottom396\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4093\fi-832\ri0\sb443\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.6 \lang1033 Frequency of Message Sends by Flavor\line (adjusted for primitive failures)}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2178\shptop29\shpright8824\shpbottom29\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv