\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-256\ri0\sb126\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx468 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Common Send. \i0 Special operations which either execute directly\line (five cases) or indirectly through the lookup of a selector in the\line special messages array. Although these bytecodes have a higher\line \expndtw7 static frequency than special arithmetic sends, they execute \lang1032 10%\line \expndtw3\lang1033 less of the time.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx468 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx468 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Selector Send.  \i0 An  instruction  specifying where the  selector  is\line \expndtw9 found in the literal frame of the compiled method. These sends\line can access the first \lang1032 16 \lang1033 literal selectors in the compiled method,\line \expndtw7 and they take \lang1032 0, 1, \lang1033 or \lang1032 2 \lang1033 arguments. The static frequency concurs\line \expndtw3 with our flavor analysis as selector send bytecodes constitute more\line \expndtw6 than \lang1032 50% \lang1033 of all sends in methods, but less than one-third of exe-\line \expndtw0 cution.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx468 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  4.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li468\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx468 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Extended Selector. \i0 These are \lang1032 2- \lang1033 and 3-byte extended versions of\line \expndtw8 the regular selector sends for greater literal access range and/or\line \expndtw5 larger numbers of arguments. They \i come \i0 in two flavors: one is an\line ordinary message send to receiver; the other starts message look-\line \expndtw4 up in the superclass of the receiver. The 2-byte version can access\line the first \lang1032 16 \lang1033 selectors with \lang1032 0 \lang1033 to \lang1032 7 \lang1033 arguments. The 3-byte version al-\line \expndtw7 locates a byte to the selector index and the argument count, with\line \expndtw9 a range of \lang1032 0 \lang1033 to \lang1032 255 \lang1033 for each. These are rarely executed so their\line \expndtw5 static frequency is triple the execution rate.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop443\shpright6646\shpbottom443\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1681\fi0\ri0\sb500\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.8 \lang1033 Send Bytecode Frequency}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa281\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2203 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3873 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5219 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx7429 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li54\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Send Bytecode}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li587\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Static \lang1032 %}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li162\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Dynamic \lang1032 %}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Cumulative}\ce