e 88.66%\line 89.94%\line 91.13%\line \expndtw-7 100.00%}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1568\margrsxn1425\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2250\shptop29\shpright8903\shpbottom29\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2239\fi0\ri22\sb407\sa540\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The statistics in Table \lang1032 12.13 \lang1033 for message lookup are for method cache\line \expndtw8 misses. Our method cache hit rate is \lang1032 93% \lang1033 for a \lang1032 509 \lang1033 element cache.\line \expndtw3 There is an average of \lang1032 3.89 \lang1033 probes into each message dictionary after a\line \expndtw4 cache miss. Combined with the superclass chain traversals, each send\line \expndtw1 missing the cache requires an average of \lang1032 8.48 \lang1033 probes of message diction-\line \expndtw4 aries, searching the message dictionaries of the class and superclass of\line \expndtw7 the receiver in the typical case. The appearance of figures over \lang1032 10 \lang1033 in\line \expndtw3 the table is the result of very long hash collision chains. If a message\line \expndtw5 dictionary is nearly full this will happen, but it is more likely that the\line \expndtw3 very simple hash function used by Smalltalk is causing many collisions.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1568\margrsxn1612\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1411\colsr1922\colno2\colw5396 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2257\shptop-58\shpright8910\shpbottom-58\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop-36\shpright1904\shpbottom-36\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWi