ottom32\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2268\fi0\ri0\sb378\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Push   instructions   can   access   four  different   memory  areas   in   the\line \expndtw3 Smalltalk-80 execution environment:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2761\fi-245\ri0\sb234\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 1. \i\lang1033 Temporary Variable. \i0 The area just above the stack in a method\line context is the temporary frame where the Smalltalk-80 language\line passes arguments and allocates local and temporary variables.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn544\margrsxn1397\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-389\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn10\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs40 \'c3}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1120\fi0\ri0\sb47\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex148\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 The Analysis of the Smalltalk^) System aTHe^Te^Packai}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3812\fi-256\ri0\sb176\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx3812 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3812\fi-256\ri0\sb176\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx3812 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Receiver Variable. \i0 The instance variables of the receiver of the\line \expndtw-2 message.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3812\fi-256\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx3812 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3812\fi-256\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx3812 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Literal Variable. \i0 A variable accessed through a pointer to an asso-\line \expndtw4 ciation in the literal frame of a compiled method.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3812\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx3812 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  4.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3812\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx3812 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Literal Constant. \i0 A constant value in the literal frame of a com-\line \expndtw1 piled method.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li3312\fi0\ri4\sb238\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Table \lang1032 12.14 \lang1033 lists the frequencies of these plus the special push instruc-\line tions for frequently used constants and environment values, such as self\line \expndtw6 (the receiver of the current message). The extended category includes\line \expndtw5 all four flavors of push instructions. The static frequencies for literal\line access are triple the execution rate, which is less than \i\lang1032 6%. \i0\lang1033 Literal con-\line \expndtw6 stant access is particularly low because of the push constant instruc-\line \expndtw1 tions for \lang1032 2, 1, 0, \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'97\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161 1, \lang1033 false, true, and nil. These seven bytecodes alone\line \expndtw3 constitute \lang1032 15.71% \lang1033 of all pushes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li3308\fi238\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The access ranges of push instructions vary. The standard temporary\line and receiver variable push instructions can access the first \lang1032 16 \lang1033 entries,\line while the literal frame pushes have a range of \lang1032 32. \lang1033 The extended push\line instructions can access up to \lang1032 64 \lang1033 entries. When this range is not enough,\line \expndtw5 other tactics are necessary. For example, to access instance variable\line \expndtw3 number \lang1032 73 \lang1033 of the receiver, we can do the following:}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3539\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx3798 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  1.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3539\fi0\ri0\sb137\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx3798 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Push self [the Oop of the receiver]}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3539\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx3798 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3539\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx3798 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Push literal constant \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'e7\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  [73]}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3539\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx3798 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3539\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx3798 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent259\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Send at:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li3301\fi0\ri25\sb212\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This takes two pushes and a primitive invocation, so one can appreciate\line \expndtw5 the value of the extended push instructions.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3272\shptop353\shpright9918\shpbottom353\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4925\fi0\ri0\sb400\sa234 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.15 \lang1033 Push Bytecode Frequency}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3834\margrsxn1462\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1742\colsr1580\colno2\colw3290 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-18\shptop-194\shpright6628\shpbottom-194\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li313\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Push Bytecode}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 temporary variable \lang1032 0\line \expndtw-1\lang1033 self (receiver)\line \expndtw2 temporary variable \lang1032 1\line \expndtw3\lang1033 temporary variable \lang1032 2\line \expndtw2\lang1033 constant \lang1032 1\line \lang1033 receiver variable \lang1032 1\line \expndtw3\lang1033 receiver variable \lang1032 0\line \expndtw4\lang1033 constant nil\line \expndtw0 extended (all)\line \expndtw3 constant \lang1032 0}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa43\sl-1\slmult0\column\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx850 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2153 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3291 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri36\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Static \lang1032 %}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li54\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Dynamic \lang1032 %}\c