to \lang1032 100% \lang1033 higher than their static figures.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2218\fi238\ri749\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The difference in execution between loads and stores on this system\line \expndtw6 is interesting. The figures for temporary and receiver variable opera-\line \expndtw7 tions are very similar. However, the extended pop and store instruc-\line \expndtw4 tions execute over eight times more frequently than extended pushes\line \expndtw1\lang1032 (24.83% \lang1033 vs. \lang1032 2.97%). \lang1033 This is because the only way to modify literal vari-\line \expndtw5 ables is through the extended pop and store instructions, whereas there\line is a separate regular bytecode for pushing literal variables. In addition,\line \expndtw3 as noted, the range of pop and store instructions is more limited, hence\line \expndtw4 forcing the use of extended instructions more frequently. Finally, pop-\line ping the stack top is almost \lang1032 500 \lang1033 times more frequent than duplicating it\line \expndtw-3\lang1032 (22.36% \lang1033 vs. \lang1032 0.05%).}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1436\margrsxn1549\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri54\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 221}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-605 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2671 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4269 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6666 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li86\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex139\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Bytecode Measurements}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-317 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw1