1033 of the\line \expndtw2 objects are instances of the top five classes. With over \lang1032 200 \lang1033 classes in the\line \expndtw9 system, this indicates that many have very few instances. In fact,\line \expndtw3\lang1032 56.48% \lang1033 of classes (excluding metaclasses) have no instances at all and\line \expndtw8 exist mainly for the behavior inherited by their subclasses; \lang1032 26.38%\line \expndtw3\lang1033 have exactly one instance (a system controller, object, or dictionary). In\line \expndtw5 all, \lang1032 76.38% \lang1033 of all classes have fewer than \lang1032 10 \lang1033 instances. This is a result\line \expndtw4 of a particular style of Smalltalk programming making extensive use of\line an existing set of basic classes and certain paradigms.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3827\margrsxn1441\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7\shptop410\shpright6653\shpbottom410\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1022\fi0\ri0\sb464\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.23 \lang1033 Classes in the System by Memory Usage}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft7\shptop32\shpright6645\shpbottom32\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li14\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa0\tx3179\tx4669 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class of Objects{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6 Percentage{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 Cumulative Percentage}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-180 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1282 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2643 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri583\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3341\posnegy130\absw0\absh2751\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\