{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 4.82%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 99.70%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1080 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2621 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri241\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 0.23%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 99.93%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-194 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1080 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2621 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri241\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 0.07%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 100.00%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1366\margrsxn1604\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2268\shptop43\shpright8921\shpbottom43\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2282\fi0\ri0\sb220\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The \i load pointer \i0 and \i store pointer \i0 routines fetch and store object point-\line \expndtw5 ers in memory. The word and byte routines deal only with non-pointer\line \lang1032 16- \lang1033 and 8-bit quantities. Because our interpreter caches the instruction\line \expndtw3 and stack pointers, the memory access figures in Table \lang1032 12.24 \lang1033 include\line \expndtw4 neither stack push/pop operations nor bytecode instruction fetch. How-\line \expndtw2 ever, those aspects of execution have well-defined behavior and are \lang1032 - \i\lang1033 iry\line \i0\expndtw3 easy to monitor. The bias introduced by such factors can be significant.\line \expndtw5 For example, if we include bytecode fetches with the other memory\line \expndtw6 accesses, the share of \i load byte \i0 operations increases from \lang1032 0.23% \lang1033 to\line \expndtw5\lang1032 16.90%. \lang1033 This bias tends to cloud the real issues (bytecode fetch, like\line \expndtw4 death and taxes, is inevitable).}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2264\fi241\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 These figures show \i load pointer \i0 dominating the memory accesses.\line \expndtw4 This is not surprising in an object-oriented memory system. Pointer ob-\line \expndtw2 ject accesses accounted for over \lang1032 87% \lang1033 of all memory traffic. The memory\line \expndtw3 system must endure nearly five accesses per bytecode, a figure which is\line \expndtw6 due partly to the experimental nature of the system. A better imple-\line \expndtw5 mentation of the interpreter could reduce the number of accesses, but\line that was not our goal.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2282\fi241\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Load and store operations occur \lang1032 40 \lang1033 times more frequently for words\line \expndtw2 than for bytes. At \lang1032 12.41% \lang1033 word accesses seem relatively high since they\line \expndtw4 are not used by the system for any common operations. Instead, the in-\line frequent but massive bit map operations are responsible for this rate of\line \expndtw-4 access.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2282\shptop270\shpright8928\shpbottom270\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3557\fi0\ri0\sb328\sa220 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.25 \lang1033 Load Pointer Operations by Class}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3655\margrsxn1604\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1648\colsr1786\colno2\colw3214 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop-191\shpright6639\shpbottom-191\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}{\pard\plain \sb0\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx3190\posnegy7\absw0\absh-230\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Percentage}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li439\fi0\ri0\sb14\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class of Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb119\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 MethodContext\line \expndtw-2 MethodDictionary\line CompiledMethod\line \expndtw-3 Array}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1354\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Cumulative Percentage}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa176\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-187 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1267 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2549 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri569\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 27.55%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li569\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 27.55%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1267 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2549 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri569\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 25.06%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li572\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 52.61%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx12