ang1032 (79)}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1655\margrsxn1397\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx3442\tlul\tx5641 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 230{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\ul0\expndtw0 .{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 The Analysis of the Smalltalk-80 System at Hewlett-Packard}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2207\fi0\ri0\sb270\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Method and block contexts comprise over \lang1032 87% \lang1033 of pointer object instan-\line \expndtw4 tiations (Table \lang1032 12.35). \lang1033 In Smalltalk, the system creates and activates a\line \expndtw6 method context for every non-primitive send, thus leading to their\line \expndtw7 prominent position in these statistics. Over \lang1032 10% \lang1033 of instantiations are\line \expndtw4 for points and rectangles. Applications use points for screen manage-\line ment, since they are the fundamental reference for graphics operations.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3841\margrsxn1401\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft11\shptop421\shpright6657\shpbottom421\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1138\fi0\ri0\sb472\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.36 \lang1033 Pointer Object Instantiations by Size}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft11\shptop36\shpright6657\shpbottom36\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb230\sa0\tx3308\tx4810 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Size of Object{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-6 Percentage{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 Cumulative Percentage}\par \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-187 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1231 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2549 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri536\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 85.28%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 85.28%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1231 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2549 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri536\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 10.99%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 96.27%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1231 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2549 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri529\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 1.93%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 98.20%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-194 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1231 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx2549 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri533\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 1.80%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx3452\posnegy115\absw0\absh857\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 100.00%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb119\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 18 \lang1033 words\line \expndtw-2\lang1032 2 \lang1033 words\line \lang1032 38 \lang1033 words\line \expndtw-1 all others \lang1032 (37)}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft18\shptop47\shpright6664\shpbottom47\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri7\sb400\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In Table \lang1032 12.36 \lang1033 note that point size objects \lang1032 (2 \lang1033 words) are more prevalent\line than the large context size \lang1032 (38 \lang1033 words). The typically short methods of\line \expndtw5 Smalltalk rarely require the deep stack provided by a large context.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi238\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The preceding tables actually underestimate the dominance of con-\line \expndtw6 texts in memory allocation. Context instantiations consume nearly \lang1032 97\line \expndtw2\lang1033 out of every \lang1032 100 \lang1033 words allocated by the system. This is because the av-\line erage context size \lang1032 (18.44 \lang1033 words) exceeds the mean size for all other ob-\line jects by \lang1032 14.52 \lang1033 words, thus boosting the context share from \lang1032 87% \lang1033 to \lang1032 97%.\line \expndtw1\lang1033 For pointer objects alone, if we exclude contexts the average object size\line \expndtw0 drops to \lang1032 3.28 \lang1033 words.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi241\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Even though bit maps are the most frequently accessed word objects,\line \expndtw1 the system creates very few of them (only \lang1032 3.69% \lang1033 of word object instan-\line \expndtw7 tiations). Floating point objects are the most frequently instantiated\line \expndtw1 word objects and their size \lang1032 (2) \lang1033 is the most popular, both at \lang1032 96.31%. \lang1033 Most\line \expndtw7 bit maps were at least \lang1032 100 \lang1033 words, but so few were created that there\line \expndtw2 was little impact on the average size of word objects. As evidence, the\line \expndtw1 average size of word objects instantiated, excluding those of size \lang1032 2, \lang1033 was\line \expndtw-3\lang1032 341.72 \lang1033 words.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3855\margrsxn1397\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4\shptop432\shpright6650\shpbottom432\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop2297\shpright6642\shpbottom2297\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1238\fi0\ri0\sb482\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.37 \lang1033 Byte Object Instantiations by Class}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4\shptop36\shpright6650\shpbottom36\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li212\fi0\ri0\sb234\sa0\tx3298\tx4799 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class of Object{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-5 Percentage{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-2 Cumulative Percentage}\pa