ain \cbpat0\ql\li590\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx749 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx-54\posnegy191\absw1584\absh-1797\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent159\pnf46}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex74\expndtw0\dn0\f46\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex74\expndtw-16\dn0\f35\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 bits}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li590\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx749 \pvpara\phcol\posnegx-54\posnegy191\absw1584\absh-1797\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex74\expndtw0\dn0\f46\cchs161\lang1032\fs20  7\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li590\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx749 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx-54\posnegy191\absw1584\absh-1797\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart2\pnindent159\pnf46}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex74\expndtw0\dn0\f46\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex74\expndtw-17\dn0\f35\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 bits}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft58\shptop22\shpright6696\shpbottom22\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3211\fi0\ri0\sb223\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Percent of Memory Reclaimed}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4039\fi0\ri2016\sb119\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 65.21%\line 83.34%\line \expndtw-5 92.42%\line \expndtw-6 95.67%\line 97.31%\line \expndtw-7 99.87%}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1445\margrsxn949\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2264\shptop22\shpright8910\shpbottom22\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2261\fi0\ri612\sb324\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The number of bits necessary for reference counts can be important, es-\line \expndtw9 pecially for those considering hardware implementations of count\line \expndtw8 caches and managers (see Chapter \lang1032 19). \lang1033 Table \lang1032 12.39 \lang1033 shows that \lang1032 4 \lang1033 bits}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1702\margrsxn1343\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5648 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 232{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 The Analysis of the Smalltalk-80 System at Hewlett-Packard}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2200\fi0\ri0\sb295\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 can reclaim over \lang1032 90% \lang1033 of memory, while \lang1032 6 \lang1033 bits can manage over \lang1032 97%.\line \expndtw7\lang1033 Because of the availability of fast byte access and arithmetic on our\line \expndtw3 host machines, our system uses an \lang1032 8 \lang1033 bit reference count field in a 16-bit\line \expndtw7 header with additional separate permanent object and count overflow\line or exemption flag bits. Using our reference-count verifier, we have\line \expndtw3 found only a few non-permanent object counts over \lang1032 255, \lang1033 while some of\line \expndtw5 the permanent kernel objects have hundreds of references.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2210\shptop425\shpright8848\shpbottom425\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2549\fi0\ri0\sb475\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.40 \lang1033 Pointer Chasing for Count Down Operations by Depth}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa274\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-194 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3010 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx4940