0 grandson decremented, \lang1032 > \lang1033 zero}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li731\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 0.18%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li464\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 99.93%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-310 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3010 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4940 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6646 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 deeper levels \lang1032 (12)}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li731\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 0.07%}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li382\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 100.00%}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2171\fi0\ri32\sb385\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The most expensive side of the dynamic memory management scheme\line \expndtw7 involves reference count decrement and the possible pointer chasing\line \expndtw5 and object deallocation. There are nearly two reference count decre-\line \expndtw2 ments for every bytecode executed. Table \lang1032 12.40 \lang1033 shows to what depth the\line \expndtw4 associated pointer chasing went during experiments with the system.\line \expndtw7 Objects with active reference counts accounted for \lang1032 24.58% \lang1033 of count\line \expndtw5 down invocations and the other \lang1032 75.42% \lang1033 were on small integers or ob-\line \expndtw4 jects exempt from count management (either permanent or count over-\line \expndtw1 flow). Only \lang1032 4.03% \lang1033 of count down invocations resulted in a decrement to\line \expndtw9 zero and a subsequent deallocation for a rate of one every \lang1032 13.61\line \expndtw2\lang1033 bytecodes. Nearly all of these deallocations caused some pointer chasing\line \expndtw1 to decrement the counts of objects referenced from the fields of the now\line \expndtw3 dead object; the average depth of such pointer chases was \lang1032 1.13 \lang1033 levels.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2203\shptop526\shpright8849\shpbottom526\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2563\fi0\ri0\sb576\sa220 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.41 \lang1033 Objects Disposed through Garbage Collection by Class}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3913\margrsxn1808\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols3\colno1\colw1209\colsr2383\colno2\colw1105\colsr558\colno3\colw932 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-14\shptop-184\shpright6639\shpbottom-184\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb245\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Class of Object}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 MethodContext}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Process}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 BlockContext}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Percentage of\line \expndtw-4 Disposed}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li166\fi0\ri364\sb119\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs2