\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-10\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 1000}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-302 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx2506 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3701 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5091 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6646 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Totals}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri461\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 214}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri421\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 269}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri396\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 11,200}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1670\margrsxn1339\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5656 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 234{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 The Analysis of the Smalltalk-80 System at Hewlett-Packard}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2236\fi238\ri0\sb284\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The code size of our system ranges from \lang1032 50 \lang1033 kilobytes in an optimized\line \expndtw2 version using procedures to \lang1032 100 \lang1033 kilobytes for the multi-level debug ver-\line \expndtw3 sion using in-line macros. The static data area ranges from \lang1032 300 \lang1033 to \lang1032 500\line \expndtw2\lang1033 kilobytes, and the dynamic allocation from \lang1032 400 \lang1033 to \lang1032 500 \lang1033 kilobytes. Total\line memory usage falls between \lang1032 750 \lang1033 kilobytes and \lang1032 1 \lang1033 megabyte. The system\line \expndtw6 installed at HP Labs has \lang1032 80 \lang1033 kilobytes of code, \lang1032 350 \lang1033 kilobytes of static\line \expndtw3 data, and \lang1032 400 \lang1033 kilobytes of dynamic data.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2210\fi238\ri4\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Throughout the implementation process, the execution profile of the\line system changed continually. At the beginning of July, the system was\line spending most of its time in the management of object memory. The top\line \expndtw1\lang1032 14 \lang1033 procedures consumed \lang1032 90% \lang1033 of execution time, and object memory\line \expndtw3 management accounted for over half of that. As the implementation\line \expndtw5 progressed, we steadily improved the performance of the most expen-\line \expndtw3 sive routines. For example, we were able to reduce the overhead of ob-\line \expndtw11 ject memory allocation and freeing to less than \lang1032 6%. \lang1033 In our latest\line \expndtw3 version, the top \lang1032 14 \lang1033 procedures consume less than two-thirds of the time\line \expndtw4 and one must add up the first \lang1032 31 \lang1033 routines to reach \lang1032 90%. \lang1033 One-quarter of\line the time is spent in bytecode fetch, event recognition, and the execution\line \expndtw0 of all bytecodes except sends. The major object memory operations of al-\line \expndtw3 location, garbage collection, and reference count management consume\line \expndtw4 another \lang1032 25%. \lang1033 The message send process takes \lang1032 25% \lang1033 of the time, includ-\line \expndtw3 ing message binding and context initialization. Finally, primitive func-\line \expndtw5 tions use the final quarter of execution time.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2232\shptop436\shpright8885\shpbottom436\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2502\fi0\ri0\sb486\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Table \lang1032 12.43 \lang1033 VAX Instructions Executed for Each Bytecode Category}\par \pard\plain\fs2\sa281\sl-1\slmult0\par\trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1987 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3535 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5025 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Bytecode Category}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li266\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Minimum}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li245\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Maximum}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li176\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Average}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-295 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1987 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3535 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5025 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 stack push}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri601\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 11}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri378\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 33}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri774\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 16}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-238 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1987 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3535 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5025 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 stack pop and store}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri590\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 2}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri382\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 47}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri774\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 28}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-230 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1987 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3535 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5025 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 return}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri590\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 43}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri385\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 81}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri774\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 46}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-252 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx1987 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx3535 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx5025 \clvertalt\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 branch and jump}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri594\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 3}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri382\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 13}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri785\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 11}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-302 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1987 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx3535 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5025 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 message send}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri594\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 33}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri378\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 >1000}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri774\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 120}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2218\fi0\ri25\sb313\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Recently we investigated the VAX assembly code generated from our C\line \expndtw3 modules. The main interpreter loop is \lang1032 12 \lang1033 instructions long. Table \lang1032 12.43\line \expndtw4\lang1033 lists the additional instructions executed for each instruction category.\line \expndtw3 The cost of maintaining contexts as separate objects plus the message\line \expndtw7 lookup process contributed heavily to the relatively high figures for\line \expndtw4 sends and returns. The 15-bit signed arithmetic required for small inte-\line \expndtw3 ger objects was also very expensive to implement on the VAX.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri29\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The performance of the system also changed substantially over the\line \expndtw8 course of several months. By the first week in July \lang1032 1981, \lang1033 our system}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3690\margrsxn1602\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx5584\posnegy122\absw0\absh-439\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 \par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 was executing around \lang1032 500 \lang1033 bytecodes per CPU second}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 memory, and over \lang1032 1000 \lang1033 bytecodes per CPU second with}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 week later we were at \lang1032 750/1500 \lang1033 bytecodes per CPU se}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 memory versions). By early September, the interpreter}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 better than \lang1032 2000 \lang1033 bytecodes per CPU second (fast memory \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'ed\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161 ^\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161 \'c9\'ef\'e7\'c3\'df\'ed\'ef}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx6019 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 weeks later it had increased to \lang1032 2800 \lang1033 bytecodes per CPU{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\i\scaps\expndtw-18 a   \i0 tv\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'ab}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx6469 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 fifth version of HP Smalltalk boosted this to \lang1032 4000 \lang1033 bytecodes \scaps d{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'e7}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20\pvpara\phcol\posnegx6332\posnegy90\absw0\absh-209\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1031\fs18  \lang1033 per}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs