dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 format a bunch of text}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri86\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 5}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri61\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 63.633}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 4030}\cell \pard\intbl\row \trowd\trgaph40 \trrh-317 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx1562 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx4111 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx5133 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6040 \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\cltxlrtb\cellx6652 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 TextEditing}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li133\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 text replacement}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri83\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 20}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri65\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 215.667}\cell \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \intbl \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 3120}\cell \pard\intbl\row \pard\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2254\fi0\ri4\sb742\sa1368\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Table \lang1032 12.44 \lang1033 gives the results of running the testStandardTests set of\line \expndtw6 benchmarks on the HP Smalltalk-84 system. Note that this is an earli-\line er version of the benchmarks than the one in the current Smalltalk-80\line \expndtw4 image. The table includes the time in seconds reported by Smalltalk for\line \expndtw5 running each entire test, and the speed of execution in bytecodes per\line \expndtw13 second. We ran the tests on a single-user VAX-11/780 with \lang1032 4\line \expndtw5\lang1033 megabytes main memory under 4.1BSD UNIX. The system was in a\line \expndtw2 normal configuration with display, keyboard, and mouse active. Clearly,\line \expndtw4 the primitive method situation is the most serious. The benchmarks for\line \expndtw2 primitive methods averaged about \lang1032 5000 \lang1033 bytecodes per second, seriously\line \expndtw4 limiting opportunities for greater speed.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1657\margrsxn1352\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1328\colsr925\colno2\colw6645 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop-248\shpright8902\shpbottom-248\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Conclusion}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb65\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Our curiosity about the Smalltalk-80 system had lead us down a prim-\line \expndtw6 rose path. When the termination of the project washed away the path,\line \expndtw3 we traded in our programming language robes for the lab coats of the\line \expndtw4 pathologist. The result of our post mortem was simple: there was little\line hope for performance high enough to lure users away from traditional\line \expndtw6 programming systems. Although we did not have the luxury of iterat-\line \expndtw3 ing and refining our implementation, the experience of those who did is\line very discouraging. No one in the test program was able to achieve per-\line \expndtw2 formance considerably above \lang1032 25 \lang1033 KIPS. Even with microcode assist, it is\line \expndtw7 difficult to imagine an implementation performing at better than \lang1032 50%\line \expndtw4\lang1033 of native mode operation. In our experience, though users like the\line functionality of a Smalltalk system, they are unwilling to accept a sig-\line \expndtw3 nificant loss in performance.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1313\margrsxn1656\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7898\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx8647 \f2\fs20{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-16\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 237}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 References}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop313\shpright8914\shpbottom313\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4\fi0\ri0\sb630\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx2264 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex142\expndtw-5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Acknowledg-{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex114\expndtw2 The analysis of the Smalltalk-80 system at Hewlett-Packard Laborato-}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx2264 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex142\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 ments{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\charscalex114\expndtw4 ries was basically a post-mortem. Nearly all of the work described in}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2261\fi0\ri32\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex114\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 this report happened after the project terminated. I appreciate the pa-\line \expndtw0 tience and understanding of my management during the period when I\line \expndtw1 spent my spare time generating and analyzing the body of statistics.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop878\shpright8914\shpbottom878\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb1213\sa0\tx2509 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex142\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 References{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\b0\sub\charscalex110\expndtw4 L\nosupersub  \sub Clark>\nosupersub  \sub D\nosupersub  \sub w\nosupersub    \sub an(J\nosupersub  \sub Leyy>\nosupersub  \sub H\nosupersub  \sub M\nosupersub    "Measurement and Analysis of In-}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2754\fi0\ri40\sb7\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 struction Use in the VAX-11/780", Proceedings of the Ninth An-\line \expndtw2 nual Symposium on Computer Architecture, pp. \lang1032 9-17, \lang1033 Austin, TX,\line \expndtw-10\lang1032 1982.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li2491\fi0\ri0\sb122\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 2. \i\lang1033 Ibid.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn10516\margrsxn360\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-4\shptop-245\shpright1155\shpbottom-245\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-680\shptop-418\shpright-680\shpbottom1051\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 2540}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Abstract}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2758\margrsxn2455\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1926\shptop-324\shpright6671\shpbottom-324\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1933\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-432\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs44 An Assessment of\line \expndtw-3 Method-Lookup Caches\line \expndtw5 for Smalltalk-80\line \expndtw9 Implementations}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1926\fi0\ri0\sb277\sa0\sl-277\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs30 Thomas J. Conroy\line \expndtw3 Eduardo Pelegri-Llopart}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1930\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Computer Science Division}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1930\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Department of Electrical Engineering and}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1922\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Computer Sciences}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1926\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 University of California, Berkeley}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-1105\shptop1159\shpright6685\shpbottom1159\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri14\sb1480\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A unique feature of the Smalltalk-80 language is the dynamic binding\line \expndtw1 of methods to a message based on the class of its receiver. This binding\line \expndtw2 requires a lookup of the selector in the message dictionaries of the su-\line perclass chain for the receiver. A way to avoid this time-consuming pro-\line \expndtw3 cess is to cache the most frequently used information. In this paper, we\line \expndtw2 present an assessment of the cost effectiveness of this mechanism. A\line \expndtw3 theoretical analysis characterizes the behavior of the cache in terms of\line \expndtw5 variables dependent on both the particular implementation and on the\line \expndtw7 Smalltalk code being executed. One result is that the benefits of the\line \expndtw6 cache heavily depend on the relation of the speed of the implementa-\line \expndtw3 tion to the speed of the cache accesses, and also on the instruction mix\line being executed. For software implementations of virtual machines, a\line \expndtw4 method-cache can greatly enhance performance. We then present the\line \expndtw3 implementation of the software method-cache in BS, the Smalltalk-80\line \expndtw5 implementation at UC Berkeley (see Chapter \lang1032 11). \lang1033 Measurements from\line \expndtw4 this implementation show that the cache increased execution speed by\line \expndtw-5\lang1032 37%.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li11\fi0\ri0\sb223\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Copyright \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032 \'a9\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  \lang1033 Thomas J. Conroy and Eduardo Pelegri-Llopart \lang1032 1982. \lang1033 All rights reserved.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb299\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 239}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1735\margrsxn1261\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx5260 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 240{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li18\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa551 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 An Assessment of Method-Lookup Caches for Smalltalk-80 Implementations}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1735\margrsxn1268\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1519\colsr716\colno2\colw6670 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop-245\shpright8907\shpbottom-245\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Introduction}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li22\fi0\ri0\sb72\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A unique feature of the Smalltalk-80 language is the dynamic binding\line \expndtw2 of methods based on the class of the receiver. Conceptually, given a re-\line ceiver and a message selector, the actions to perform are\super 1\nosupersub\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f3\cchs0 \'b7\super\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0 2\nosupersub :}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li259\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa0\tx515 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-18\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  1.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li259\fi0\ri0\sb227\sa0\tx515 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-18\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Determine the class of the receiver,}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li515\fi-256\ri0\sb112\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx515 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  2.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li515\fi-256\ri0\sb112\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx515 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-12\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Search for the message selector in the message dictionaries of the\line \expndtw4 receiver's superclass chain, and}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li515\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx515 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  3.\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li515\fi-256\ri0\sb115\sa0\sl-238\slmult0\tx515 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent256\pnf25{\pntxta .}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-13\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Retrieve the method associated with the message selector in the\line \expndtw3 dictionary where the search succeeded.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li18\fi0\ri0\sb234\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A direct implementation of this \i lookup \i0 process is time-consuming since\line \expndtw2 a large number of bytecodes involve method-lookup. A solution to this\line \expndtw1 problem is to \i cache\super 3\nosupersub  \i0 the result of the whole lookup process. A cache can\line \expndtw4 provide a fast by-pass of the lengthy search.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi238\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A method cache stores combinations of receivers and message selec-\line tors, allowing look-ups to be retrieved quickly when the combinations\line \expndtw7 needed for the look-up are in the cache. For those combinations not\line \expndtw5 found in the cache, a full look-up has to be done. An additional over-\line head present in caching is the cost of trying to keep the more frequent-\line \expndtw3 ly required combinations on the cache. Clearly, the feasibility of this\line \expndtw6 technique depends on how often the bypass succeeds and the relative\line \expndtw3 cost of each alternative.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi230\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The effect of the technique on the performance of an implementation\line \expndtw3 is related to the cost of look-ups, the cost of the remaining components\line \expndtw5 and the relative occurrence of each part. In this short paper we present\line \expndtw4 an assessment of this cache mechanism using a simple theoretical anal-\line \expndtw10 ysis and measurements from a software implementation of the\line \expndtw3 Smalltalk-80 virtual machine, (see Chapter \lang1032 11).}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1735\margrsxn1261\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb1145\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1735\margrsxn1261\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1029\colsr1228\colno2\colw6656 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft0\shptop-252\shpright8914\shpbottom-252\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Analysis}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb61\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 This analysis compares the behavior of a straightforward implementa-\line tion of a Smalltalk-80 virtual machine to an implementation with a\line method-cache. Subscripted capital letters represent virtual machine im-\line \expndtw7 plementation-dependent quantities, while greek letters represent\line \expndtw2 Smalltalk-80 code-dependent quantities. Specifically,}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li436\fi-194\ri0\sb234\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx436 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li436\fi-194\ri0\sb234\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx436 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent194\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 A \i0 with a subscript represents the time for completing a method\line \expndtw-3 look-up,}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li241\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\tx436 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li241\fi0\ri0\sb101\sa0\tx436 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnstart-1\pnindent195\pnf25{\pntxtb \'95}}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 S represents the number of bytecodes/second (speed), and}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn3856\margrsxn1357\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1951\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx6408 \f2\fs20{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-14\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 241}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Analysis}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li454\fi-205\ri0\sb263\sa0\sl-241\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 \'95\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161   \i\lang1033 F \i0 represents the fraction of total time spent in doing method-look-\line \expndtw-4 ups.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li14\fi0\ri18\sb230\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 We stress the distinction between Smalltalk-80 code-dependent and im-\line \expndtw4 plementation-dependent quantities because the former are constants in-\line dependent of the implementation. For example, implementations may\line \expndtw6 differ drastically in the number of bytecodes executed per second, but\line \expndtw5 for the same Smalltalk-80 code, the number of method-lookups per\line \expndtw2 bytecode would be identical. The following table lists the variables used\line \expndtw4 and their definitions.}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft29\shptop212\shpright6689\shpbottom212\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 6985}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li32\fi0\ri0\sb241\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Table \lang1032 13.1 \lang1033 Parameters and Definitions}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft29\shptop29\shpright6689\shpbottom29\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 4445}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li32\fi0\ri0\sb216\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 Implementation Dependent Values}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb126\sa0\tx1084 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs20 A{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw2 method lookup time for a cache miss*}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li173\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tx2228 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs14 miss{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw0\lang1032 "}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tx1084 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex94\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 A\sub n{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\nosupersub\expndtw16 method lookup time without a cache}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx1084 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex94\expndtw-6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 A\sub hit{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\nosupersub\expndtw16 method lookup time for a cache hit}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li29\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex94\expndtw16\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Implementation and Smalltalk Code Dependent Values}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-356\slmult0\tx1080 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex94\expndtw-11\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 \'c1\sub \'f7\'ca{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\nosupersub\expndtw17\hich\af1\dbch\af3\loch\f1\cchs0\lang1033 average method lookup time for an xK entry method cache}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx1080 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex94\expndtw-12\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 S\sub nc{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\nosupersub\expndtw15 number of bytecodes/sec without a cache}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-234\slmult0\tx1080 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex94\expndtw-15\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 S\sub xK{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\nosupersub\expndtw16 number of bytecodes/sec with an xK entry method cache}\par 