i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure \lang1032 15.5}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb18\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure \lang1032 15.6}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1458\margrsxn1509\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2300\fi0\ri22\sb1519\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 users. In the Smalltalk-80 system, this usually occurs when two pro-\line \expndtw4 grammers have modified the same Smalltalk method definition.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2290\fi234\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In order to help solve this problem, we developed a program for ana-\line \expndtw5 lyzing Smalltalk-80 code files and reporting the ways in which they\line \expndtw10 conflict, i.e., by modifying the same method definition or other\line \expndtw3 Smalltalk object. This approach works very well since most Smalltalk\line \expndtw4 method definitions are very short and perform a very specific function.\line \expndtw3 Whenever two or more submissions define the same method, all con-\line \expndtw4 flicting definitions are appended to a "conflict report" file. It is then up\line \expndtw3 to the programmers involved to determine how to resolve the conflicts.\line \expndtw4 Often one of the definitions can be chosen over the others. Otherwise a}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1524\margrsxn1449\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4176\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx8651 \f2\fs20{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 279}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex139\expndtw-1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 An On-Line System Development Database}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2279\fi0\ri0\sb252\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw4\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 new method must be written which merges or resolves the functionality\line \expndtw3 of the conflicting definitions. No automatic conflicts resolution was\line \expndtw4 attempted.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2268\fi238\ri7\sb0\sa1361\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Although this tool is fairly crude, it has proven very useful for\line \expndtw4 detecting and resolving at least some conflicts which otherwise would\line have gone undetected or surfaced later as annoying bugs.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1524\margrsxn1464\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1573\colsr673\colno2\colw6674 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft4\shptop-313\shpright8932\shpbottom-313\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 An On-Line\line \expndtw-2 System\line Development\line \expndtw0 Database}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw9\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 After using the interim support mechanism for several months, we\line \expndtw10 were ready to create a development support system within the\line \expndtw3 Smalltalk-80 system itself. Since the Smalltalk-80 system did not then\line \expndtw8 interface with the Xerox internal electronic mail system, one of the\line \expndtw5 main disadvantages of the interim mechanism was that users were not\line able to submit reports directly from the Smalltalk-80 system. In addi-\line \expndtw4 tion to allowing users to submit bug reports and software submissions\line \expndtw5 directly from within the Smalltalk-80 system, we wanted the new sys-\line \expndtw4 tem to provide a Smalltalk-style user interface for browsing, adding to,\line \expndtw3 and editing the system development database. Fig. \lang1032 15.7 \lang1033 shows the com-\line ponents of the current support system involved in submitting a bug fix.\line \expndtw7 The new database, like the mail files of the interim system, resides\line \expndtw3 in a number of data files on a remote file server, accessible to any run-\line \expndtw13 ning Smalltalk-80 system. Since the database is accessed by\line \expndtw9 Smalltalk-80 systems rather than standard mail programs, we were\line \expndtw3 able to automatically include additional information, such as cross ref-\line \expndtw5 erences between related entries in the database.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2874\margrsxn1763\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb1040\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2874\margrsxn1763\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols3\colno1\colw1832\colsr306\colno2\colw2347\colsr302\colno3\colw2484 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft122\shptop-72\shpright1598\shpbottom-72\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2563\shptop-72\shpright4075\shpbottom-72\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5011\shptop-65\shpright7322\shpbottom-65\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri18\sb18\sa0\sl-158\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 user fixes a bug and   \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f24\cchs161\lang1032 \'cb}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-158\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 places the code file      \lang1032 )}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri18\sb0\sa0\sl-158\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-4\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 ^ona remote file server/}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-158\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-1\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 (user \i0 submits a bug fix \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f24\cchs161\lang1032 \'cb}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-158\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 *   \lang1033 I   report describing the    \lang1032 )   '}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qc\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-158\slmult0\tx734\tx1714 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw52\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 \\^{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\expndtw-8 bug fix{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\i\expndtw0 y}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li32\fi0\ri22\sb72\sa0\sl-158\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 /the VersionHandler adds \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f24\cchs161\lang1032 \'cb\line \expndtw-4\hich\af0\dbch\af24\loch\f0\cchs161 ( \lang1033 an entry to the appropriate \lang1032 )\line \expndtw1\lang1033 V^ remote database file     \i J}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1087\fi0\ri0\sb25\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 Jj}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb43\sa0\sl-162\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-6\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 f   \i0 user opens a changes browser\line \expndtw-5\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f24\cchs161\lang1032 \'df\hich\af0\dbch\af24\loch\f0\cchs161    \lang1033 and may inspect, modify, \i or\line \i0\expndtw0 \\incorporate database entries}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2399\margrsxn2137\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb184\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2399\margrsxn2137\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols4\colno1\colw1087\colsr619\colno2\colw1706\colsr695\colno3\colw784\colsr835\colno4\colw1645 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft1750\shptop-29\shpright3327\shpbottom-29\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5767\shptop-22\shpright7344\shpbottom-22\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft3917\shptop583\shpright3917\shpbottom885\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5054\shptop583\shpright5054\shpbottom885\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb677\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure \lang1032 15.7}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-7\dn0\f24\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 ( \lang1033 Smalltalk-80 System]}\par {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft36\shptop0\shpright1606\shpbottom0\shpfhdr0\shpbxcolumn\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li742\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0\sl-421\slmult0\tlul\tx1706 \f2\fs20{\b\i0\cf0\charscalex224\expndtw0\dn6\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs52 I{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb623\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-9\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 File Server}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f2\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 (smalltalk-80 System\ul0 )}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1482\margrsxn1496\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li7\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx4565 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 280{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa554 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Managing the Evolution of Smalltalk-80 Systems}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1496\margrsxn1503\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1562\colsr680\colno2\colw6667 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-7\shptop-306\shpright8907\shpbottom-306\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 Structure of\line \expndtw8 the Database}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi0\ri7\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw8\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The current version handler database is patterned strongly after the\line \expndtw4 mail files used in the interim system. The database contains three\line \expndtw1 kinds of entries: \i system versions, bug reports, \i0 and \i system changes \i0 (in-\line \expndtw7 cluding bug fixes and "goodies"). Each entry has a unique ID, and a\line \expndtw4 user supplied title and message body describing the entry. The system\line \expndtw3 adds fields specifying the date and the version of the Smalltalk-80 sys-\line \expndtw5 tem from which the entry has been generated. Additional fields may\line \expndtw4 contain various status conditions of the entry. Most fields are stored as\line \expndtw6 text in the header portion of the message; some special fields (e.g.,\line \expndtw8 whether an entry is new or old or has been deleted) are hidden from\line \expndtw4 the user.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi245\ri7\sb4\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 System version \i0 entries also contain the ID's of the \i system changes\line \i0\expndtw2 which differentiate the version from its predecessor. Thus a new version\line \expndtw3 can be generated from some previous version by automatically incorpo-\line \expndtw4 rating the appropriate changes into the user's Smalltalk-80 image. Ver-\line \expndtw1 sion entries also contain the ID's of all \i bug reports \i0 which apply to that\line \expndtw-1 version.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li7\fi241\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 In addition to containing a description of the bug, \i bug report \i0 entries\line \expndtw4 contain the ID's of available \i system changes \i0 that fix the bug.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li11\fi245\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw2\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 System change \i0 entries contain the names of one or more remote files\line containing Smalltalk-80 source code. If the change fixes a reported bug,\line \expndtw4 the change entry also contains the ID of the corresponding bug report\line \expndtw3 entry. No firm distinction is made between submissions which are actu-\line \expndtw4 ally changes or fixes to the Smalltalk-80 system and arbitrary user ap-\line \expndtw7 plications (i.e., goodies). Some changes get incorporated into later\line \expndtw3 versions of the system while others simply remain in the database for\line \expndtw4 optional retrieval.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi238\ri11\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw18\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The database is maintained by a special object, named\line \expndtw11 VersionHandler, which is in every Smalltalk-80 system. The\line \expndtw4 VersionHandler object acts as an interface to the actual database stored\line \expndtw6 on a remote file server. It is responsible for reading and writing por-\line \expndtw11 tions of the database and coordinating access among multiple\line \expndtw2 Smalltalk-80 systems.}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1507\margrsxn1496\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 {\pard\plain \sb1084\sa0\sl-1\slmult0\fs2\par}\sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1507\margrsxn1496\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols2\colno1\colw1278\colsr979\colno2\colw6649 {\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft-25\shptop-299\shpright8896\shpbottom-299\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\sl-238\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs28 A Browser\line \expndtw6 Style User\line \expndtw9 Interface}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li4\fi0\ri0\sb7\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The user creates Smalltalk windows for accessing the database by send-\line \expndtw1 ing Smalltalk messages to the VersionHandler. The top level commands\line \expndtw4 available to the user for accessing the database include:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li238\fi0\ri0\sb223\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 \'95\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161   \lang1033 Open a version browser}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2329\margrsxn1544\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li3272\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx7751 \f2\fs20{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw-5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs20 281}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qr\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex140\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 A Browser Style User Interface}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1602\fi0\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-353\slmult0\tx1807 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs22  \'95\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li1602\fi0\ri0\sb122\sa0\sl-353\slmult0\tx1807 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\