st \shpleft1706\shptop-2408\shpright1706\shpbottom213\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft2081\shptop-1832\shpright2081\shpbottom220\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 11430}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft6091\shptop-2689\shpright6091\shpbottom220\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 29845}}}}{\shp {\*\shpinst \shpleft5681\shptop-2394\shpright5681\shpbottom220\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbypara\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shpz0\shplid1{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 13970}}}}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb11\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw6\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Figure \lang1032 15.8}\par \column \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex110\expndtw10\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs12 VersionHandler submitGoodie}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn2329\margrsxn1544\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1339\fi0\ri32\sb356\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Each of these commands causes a new window to be created. There are\line \expndtw11 three kinds of database browsers for the three kinds of database\line \expndtw5 records: version browsers, change browsers and bug report browsers.\line \expndtw6 These browsers differ only in their contents and the command menus\line \expndtw4 they provide. Fig. \lang1032 15.9 \lang1033 shows a version browser in which the user is\line \expndtw3 selecting the browse changes command. Fig. \lang1032 15.10 \lang1033 shows the changes\line \expndtw4 browser created as a result of the selection.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1339\fi238\ri25\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw1\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Fig. \lang1032 15.11 \lang1033 shows the command menus provided by each kind of brows-\line \expndtw5 er. Selecting browse changes creates a browser on the changes which\line \expndtw6 make up the version. The browse goodies command creates a browser\line \expndtw4 on all changes which are \i not \i0 included in the current version. This is\line \expndtw3 equivalent to searching an applications library of user programs and op-\line \expndtw4 tional system enhancements. The retrieve version command is useful if\line \expndtw3 the version of the Smalltalk-80 system one is running is not the most re-\line \expndtw2 cent. By selecting retrieve version, the user can upgrade the system. The\line \expndtw5 system then automatically retrieves all the required changes.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li1354\fi230\ri18\sb4\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 The browse source files and file in changes commands in the changes\line \expndtw6 browser are similar to the special commands provided by the interim\line \expndtw4 mail browser. File in changes allows a user to incorporate a bug fix or\line other change into the Smalltalk-80 system.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1696\margrsxn1278\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li22\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx4586 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\ul\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw-14\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs16 282{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li25\fi0\ri0\sb4\sa0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex132\expndtw5\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs16 Managing the Evolution of Smalltalk-80 Systems}\par \sect\sectd \sbknone\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn6613\margrsxn1278\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \li0\ri0\sb0\sa0\pvpara\phmrg\posnegx-4954\posnegy302\absw0\absh5962\nowrap\dfrmtxtx40\dfrmtxty0 {\pict\picw7912\pich10515\picwgoal4485\pichgoal5961\jpegblip
