n \cbpat0\ql\li4554\fi-616\ri0\sb58\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx4554 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18  10\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4554\fi-616\ri0\sb58\sa0\sl-241\slmult0\tx4554 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart10\pnindent616\pnf25}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw5\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw3\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 The special primitive "return a field from within Self". In\line \expndtw2 this case the primitive index can be used to indicate which\line \expndtw-5 field.}\par {\pntext\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4554\fi-616\ri0\sb43\sa0\sl-245\slmult0\tx4554 \b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18  11\tab}\pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li4554\fi-616\ri0\sb43\sa0\sl-245\slmult0\tx4554 \f2\fs20{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pndec\pnstart10\pnindent616\pnf25}\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw0\dn0\f25\cchs161\lang1032\fs18 {\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw7\dn0\f3\cchs0\lang1033\fs18 An ordinary primitive.  In this case the primitive index\line \expndtw0 tells which one.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat0\qj\li2261\fi0\ri14\sb335\sa0\sl-234\slmult0 \f2\fs20{\b0\i0\cf0\charscalex100\expndtw12\dn0\loch\af1\dbch\af25\hich\f1\cchs161\lang1032\fs22 \u9633\'3f\hich\af1\dbch\af25\loch\f1\cchs161  \i\lang1033 Contexts \i0 The other two system-types are Method Context and\line \expndtw4 Block Context. The Smalltalk Method Context is the activation record\line \expndtw3 that results from a message being sent to a receiving object, and corre-\line sponds to the standard Ada Context object. Unlike the Ada Context ob-\line \expndtw6 ject however, Smalltalk Method Contexts are allocated from a global\line \expndtw5 heap and can persist after they return. The format of a Method Context\line \expndtw1 is shown in Fig. \lang1032 17.3.}\par \sect\sectd \sbkpage\pgwsxn11909\pghsxn16834\marglsxn1910\margrsxn1950\margtsxn1440\margbsxn720\cols1\colsx60 \pard \plain \cbpat0\ql\li5857\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0\tlul\tx7769 \f2\fs20{\charscal